T4 · Numbers − · Assessed value 0
POST /api/v1/training/rpt-bills pin <PIN 2>, assessed_value "0"
→ 422 {"detail":{"assessed_value":"must be greater than 0"}}

T5 · Numbers − · 3 decimals
POST /api/v1/training/rpt-bills pin <PIN 2>, assessed_value "1000.005"
→ 422 {"detail":{"assessed_value":"must be a positive amount with at most 2 decimals"}}

T6 · Syntax − · PIN with 4 groups
POST /api/v1/training/rpt-bills pin "603-26-482-100", assessed_value "1000.00"
→ 422 {"detail":{"pin":"must match NNN-NN-NNN-NNN-NNN"}}

T9 · Numbers − · One centavo over the limit
POST /api/v1/training/rpt-bills pin <PIN 2>, assessed_value "1000000000.00"
→ 422 {"detail":{"assessed_value":"must not exceed 999999999.99"}}

T7 · Claims − · Same PIN a second time
POST /api/v1/training/rpt-bills pin <PIN>, assessed_value "1000000.00"
→ 409 {"detail":{"pin":"already taken for this tenant"}}

T2 · Core + · See my bill
GET /api/v1/training/rpt-bills/{bill_id}
→ 200 property_class "INDUSTRIAL", assessed_value "1000000.00", tax_year 2026, due_date "2026-12-31", RPT 20000.00 OPEN, RPT_SEF 10000.00 OPEN

T8 · Users − · Another user asks for my bill
GET /api/v1/training/rpt-bills/{bill_id} with X-User-ID: <you>-probe
→ 404 {"detail":"Not Found"}
